<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to announce sugar crop plan by end-April.</title>
<headline>Brazil to announce sugar crop plan by end-April.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 sugar crop plan is on schedule to be published by the end of this month, said the head of the sugar and alcohol department of the Industry and Commerce Ministry.</p>
<p>&quot;The minister wants to announce the crop plan by April 30,&quot; said Pedro Cabral.</p>
<p>The department is currently evaluating estimates by individual states on sugarcane, sugar and alcohol production. However it is still awaiting a breakdown from Sao Paulo state which so far has just sent an estimate of overall cane output.</p>
<p>A technical meeting will be held on April 16 in Brasilia to discuss the figures, Cabral said.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
